            <ArticleTitle>[Oral administration of medicines in elderly patients and adaptation of galenic forms].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1268-6034(17)30129-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.sger.2017.06.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Physiological ageing and pathologies can have an influence on the pharmacology of numerous medicines, leading to serious iatrogenic accidents, polypharmacy and incorrect use of a medicine in elderly people. An observational study carried out in a short-stay geriatric unit focused on the issues surrounding the difficulties the elderly may encounter when taking medicines and the prevalence of the manipulation of galenic forms.</AbstractText>
